Your project uses **MSTest v3 (3.8.0)** on net8.0. Here's what upgrading to **MSTest v4 (4.1.0)** will break and how to fix it:

### Breaking change in your code

**`[ExpectedException]` removed** (lines 9, 18) — Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

Same pattern for `Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation`.

### Other breaking changes to be aware of (not in your code today)

| Change | Fix |
|--------|-----|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` removed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` |
| `Assert.AreEqual` with format string + params | Use string interpolation |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Just use `[ClassCleanup]` |
| `TestContext.Properties.Contains()` | Use `.ContainsKey()` |
| `[Timeout(TestTimeout.Infinite)]` | Use `[Timeout(int.MaxValue)]` |
| Custom `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` | Override `ExecuteAsync` instead |
| `TestCase.Id` changed | Azure DevOps history will re-baseline |
| `TreatDiscoveryWarningsAsErrors` now `true` | Fix discovery warnings or set to `false` |

